hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3961","Hanad bin Al-Sari Al-Kufi reported, on the authority of Abu Muhyah Al-Kufi, on the authority of Salamah bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, meaning Ibn Yazid, who said: “It was said: According to Abdullah bin Masoud, people throw the Jamarat from above Al-Aqaba. He said: Abdullah threw it from the bottom of the valley, then he said: From here. “And by Him there is no god but Him, he shot the one to whom Surah Al-Baqarah was revealed.”"
"3962","Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani and Malik bin Al-Khalil Al-Basri reported, saying: Ibn Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Mansour, On the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, he said: “Abdullah stoned the Jamarat with seven pebbles, placed the House on his left, and set aside To his right, he said: This is the abode of the one to whom Surat Al-Baqarah was revealed. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3963","Mujahid bin Musa Al-Baghdadi reported, on the authority of Hushaym, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid told us, he said: “I saw Ibn Masoud stoned Jamarat al-Aqaba, meaning from the bottom of the valley, then he said: This, by the One besides Whom there is no god, is the place of the one to whom Surat Al-Baqarah was revealed.”"
"3964","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim Al-Dawraqi told us, he said: Ibn Abi Zaida told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, he said: I heard Al-Hajjaj is Ibn Yusuf. He says: Do not say Surah Al-Baqarah, say: The Surah in which the cow is mentioned. So I mentioned that to Abraham, and he said: Abdul Rahman bin Al-Baqarah told me. Yazid said, “He was with Abdullah when he stoned the Aqaba, so he went further into the valley and looked at it, meaning Jamarat, and he threw seven pebbles, saying “Allahu Akbar.” With every pebble, so I said: People are ascending the mountain, and he said: Here, by the One besides Whom there is no god, I saw the one to whom Surah Al-Baqarah was revealed, throwing his stones.”"
"3965","Muhammad ibn Adam al-Masisi reported, on the authority of Abd al-Rahim, who is Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, and another reported, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned the Jamarat like gravel.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3966","Muhammad ibn Bashar reported, saying: Yahya al-Qattan told us, saying: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned the stones like gravel.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3967","Ibrahim bin Harun told me, he said: Hatim bin Ismail told us, he said: Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Hussein told us, on the authority of his father, he said We entered upon Jabir bin Abdullah, and I said, “Tell me about the proof of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” He said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him.” He threw seven pebbles at the Jamarat that was by the tree, saying “Allahu Akbar” with each pebble of the stone he had taken, so he stoned from the bottom of the valley, then He went to the place of slaughter and slaughtered.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3968","Yahya bin Musa reported from Khat al-Balkhi, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, Mujahid said: Saad said: “We returned from the Hajj with... The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and some of us said: I threw seven, and some of us said: I threw six, so they did not criticize one another.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3969","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala al-San’ani narrated, saying: Khaled narrated to us, saying: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of Qatada, saying: I heard Abu Majliz, saying: We asked Ibn Abbas about something about the Jamarat, and he said: “I do not know whether the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned them with six or seven stones.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3970","Harun bin Ishaq Al-Hamdani Al-Kufi told me, he said: Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali bin Hussein, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of his brother Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, he said: “I was the servant of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he continued to recite the talbiyah until he stoned Jamarat. Aqaba and he stoned it with seven pebbles, saying “Allahu Akbar” with each pebble. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3971","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Khasif, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Al-Fadl bin Abbas said: “I was a The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and I continued to hear him say the Talbiyah until he stoned Jamarat al-Aqaba. When he threw the Talbiyah, he broke off the Talbiyah.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3972","Hilal bin Al-Ala bin Hilal told me, he said: Husayn told us, he is Ibn Ayyash, he said: Abu Khaythamah told us, and his name is Zuhair bin Muawiyah, He said: Khasif told us, on the authority of Mujahid, Ata’, and Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, that Al-Fadl told him: “He was the companion of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not stop reciting the Talbiyah until he stoned the Jamarat.”"
"3973","Abu Asim Khushish bin Asram reported, on the authority of Ali bin Ma’abad, who said: Musa bin Ayan told us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Al-Fadl ibn Abbas, “He was the companion of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he continued to recite the Talbiyah until he stoned a Jamarat.” \"The obstacle\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3974","Al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem Al-Anbari Al-Basri narrated, saying: Othman bin Omar narrated to us, saying: Yunus narrated, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: “We were informed that When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stoned the Jamarat which is next to the mosque in Mina, he would throw seven pebbles at it, saying “Allahu Akbar” every time he threw it. With a pebble, then he moved in front of it and stood facing the house, raising his hands and supplicating for a long time, then he came to the second Jamarat and stoned it. With seven pebbles, he says “Allahu Akbar” whenever he throws a pebble, then he goes back to the left and stands facing the House, raising his hands, supplicating, then throwing the stone. He stones the Jamarat near Aqaba with seven pebbles. He says “Allahu Akbar” every time he throws a pebble, then he leaves and does not stop there.” Al-Zuhri said: I heard Salim narrating this on the authority of his father, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Ibn Umar used to do it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3975","Amr bin Ali reported to Abu Hafs, he said: Yahya told us, he is the son of Sa’id al-Qattan, on the authority of Sufyan, he is the son of Sa’id al-Thawri, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Al-Hasan Al-Urni, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “If he stones the Jamarat, then everything is permissible for him except women. He was asked about perfume? He said: As for me, I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, smearing himself with musk. Is he good?"
"3976","Ismail bin Masoud told us, he said: Bishr, who is Ibn al-Mufaddal, told us, he said: Abdullah bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra, on the authority of Abi Bakra, who said: He mentioned the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “He stood on his camel.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3977","Humayd bin Masada reported in his hadith, on the authority of Yazid bin Zuray’, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Tomorrow, on the authority of his father, he said: “When that day came when he was riding his camel, he said: What day is this? He said: So we remained silent until we thought He will give it another name. He said: Is it not the Day of Sacrifice? We said: Yes. He said: What month is this? We remained silent until we thought that he would name it. He changed its name. He said: Isn’t it Dhul-Hijjah? We said: Yes. He said: What country is this? We remained silent until we thought that he would call it something other than its name. “Isn’t it in the town?” We said: “Yes.” He said: “Your blood, your property, and your honor among yourselves are as sacred as the sacredness of this day of your month.” In this country of yours, this is not to inform the absent witness, for perhaps the witness will inform someone who is more knowledgeable than him.” The word is Praiseworthy (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3978","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Amir told us, he said: Qurrah bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin told me. Abu Bakra, and a better man than myself than Abdul Rahman, Humaid bin Abdul Rahman, both of them, on the authority of Abu Bakra, he said: “We engaged The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the Day of Sacrifice, and he said: Your blood and your wealth are sacred among you, just as this day of yours is sacred in your month. This is in this country of yours until the day you meet your Lord. Have I not conveyed the message? They said: Yes. He said: O God, bear witness. The witness among you will convey to the absent. Perhaps the One who conveys the message is more aware than the listener. “Won’t you return to being infidels after me, some of you striking the necks of one another?” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3979","Abdul Rahman bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Marwan told us, he said: Hilal bin Amir Al-Muzani told us, he said: I heard Rafi’ bin Amr Al-Muzani said, “He came with his father on the day of the Farewell Pilgrimage. He said: And the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was delivering a sermon to the people on a brown-brown mule.” And Ali expresses it as the Day of Sacrifice, until the dawn rose at Mina. He said: So I tore my hand from my father and passed through the men and the people, standing and sitting. So I hit his knee with both hands until I took hold of the shin of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, then I wiped them until I inserted my hand between the sandal. And the foot, it seems to me that I find the cold of his foot right on my hand.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3980","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Abu Nuh Abd al-Rahman bin Ghazwan told us, he said: Ikrimah bin Ammar told us, on the authority of Al-Harmas bin Ziyad said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a camel, giving the sermon on the Day of Eid al-Adha.”"
"3981","Ishaq bin Mansour reported, he said: Abu Usama reported, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of his brother, on the authority of Abu Kahil Abdullah bin Malik. He said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, delivering a sermon to a camel, with an Abyssinian slave holding its reins.”"
"3982","Ayoub bin Muhammad Al-Wazzan told us, he said: Marwan bin Muawiyah Al-Fazari told us, he said: Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i told us, he said: Nabit bin Al-Ashja’i’s tape, he said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, addressing the people in Mina, and he thanked God and praised Him, then he asked them and said: What? Which day was it forbidden? They said: This day. He said: Which country was it forbidden? They said: This country. He said: Which month was it forbidden? They said: This month. He said: Your blood and your wealth are as sacred to you as the sacredness of this day, the sacredness of this month, and the sacredness of this country. Oh God, Did I convey it? They said: Yes. He said: Oh God, bear witness. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3983","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed and Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Yahya, who is Ibn Sa’id, told us: Thawr told us, he said: Rashid bin Saad told us. On the authority of Abdullah bin Luhay, on the authority of Abdullah bin Qart, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The greatest of days in the sight of God is the Day of Sacrifice and the Day of Resurrection”"
"3984","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: Amr bin Murrah told me, he said: I once heard Al-Hamdani said: A man from the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, rose among us riding a camel. A bright red color. He said: Do you know what day this is? We said: The Day of Sacrifice. He said: You are right. It is the greatest day of Hajj. Do you know? Which month is this of yours? We said, and Bundar said: They said: We said: Dhul-Hijjah. He said: You are right, God’s deaf month. Do you know which month? This country of yours? We said: The Sacred Country. He said: You are right. Then he said: Your blood and your wealth are as sacred to you as this day of yours is sacred. This is your month in your country. Indeed, I will leave you at the basin, and I will gloat over you to the nations, so do not disgrace my face. Have you not seen me? And you have heard from me, and you will be asked about me. So whoever lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3985","Hanad bin Al-Sirri reported, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Ibn Garqada, on the authority of Suleiman bin Amr, on the authority of his father, who said: “I witnessed the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace, in the Farewell Pilgrimage, he says: O people, three times, what day is this? They said: The Day of Sacrifice, the day of the greatest Hajj. He said: Your blood, your property, and your honor among yourselves are as sacred as this day of yours in this country of yours. Should a criminal not commit injustice against his own child? And no child is dependent on his father. Indeed, Satan has despaired of ever being worshiped in this country of yours, but there will be obedience to him in some of the things you despise. Your deeds and He will be satisfied. Verily, every usury of the pre-Islamic times will be credited to you. Your capital will not be wronged nor will you be wronged. Indeed, every blood of The blood of the pre-Islamic period is put away, and the first thing I put away from it is the blood of Al-Harith bin Abdul-Muttalib. He was breast-feeding among the Banu Layth and Hudhayl killed him. Did Did I convey the message three times? They said: Yes. He said: O God, bear witness."
"3986","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ reported, saying: Zaid ibn al-Hubab told us, saying: Ayyash ibn Uqba informed me, saying: Khair ibn Nu’aym informed me, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, On the authority of Jabir, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “By dawn {1} and ten nights {2}, he said: The ten days of sacrifice, and Witr is the day Arafat, and the intercession on the Day of Sacrifice.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3987","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Abdul-Ala told us, he said: Hisham told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, “that the Messenger God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, stoned Jamarat al-Aqaba, then he went to the body and slaughtered it while the barber was sitting, so he nodded to his head and said: “Shave,” so he shaved his right side and divided it among those next to him, then he said: “Shave the other side.” So he shaved it and said: “Where is Abu Talha?” so he handed it to him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3988","Amr bin Mansour reported, saying: Al-Mu’alla bin Asad narrated to us, saying: Wahib narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he was told, “On the Day of Sacrifice while he was in Mina, in slaughtering, shaving, stoning, and offering sacrifice, And the delay, and he said: “There is nothing wrong.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3989","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Hushaym told us, saying: Mansour reported, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked About someone who shaved his head before he slaughtered, or slaughtered before stoning the stone, and then started saying: “There is no harm, there is no harm.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3990","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Affan told us, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Qais bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, “Indeed, a man said: Oh Messenger of God, I slaughtered before I slaughtered. He said: Shoot and there is no harm. Another said: O Messenger of God, I slaughtered before I slaughtered. He said: Slay. There is no embarrassment. Another said: I circumambulated the Kaaba, O Messenger of God, before I slaughtered. He said: Sacrifice and there is no embarrassment."
"3991","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked Peace and blessings of God be upon him, on the authority of a man who shaved his head before he slaughtered. He said: Slay and there is no harm. Another said: I slaughtered before stoning. He said: Slay and there is no harm. \" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3992","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Ghandar told us, he said: Muammar told us, he said: Ibn Shihab reported, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, standing on his camel in Mina, and a man came to him and said: O Messenger of God, I used to see That the shave is before slaughtering, so I shaved before slaughtering. He said: Slay and there is no harm. Then another came to him and said: O Messenger of God, I was I think that slaughtering should be performed before stoning, so I slaughtered before stoning. He said: Shoot and there is no problem. He was never asked about something that a man had done before except that he said: Do it. And there is no embarrassment.”"
"3993","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Malik told us, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Issa bin Talha, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood during the Farewell Pilgrimage, and a man said: O Messenger of God, I shaved before I slaughtered. He said: There is no harm.” He was never asked about anything that was brought forward or delayed except that he said: “There is no problem.”"
"3994","Ahmad ibn Amr ibn al-Sarh reported, saying: Ibn Wahb reported, saying: Malik told me, and Yunus ibn Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Issa ibn Talha bin Ubayd Allah told him: On the authority of Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-Aas, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stopped for the people in the year of Hajj.” They asked him for farewell, and a man came and said: O Messenger of God, I did not feel it, so I slaughtered myself before shooting. He said: Shoot and do not be embarrassed. Another said: O Messenger of God, I did not feel it, so I shaved before I slaughtered. He said: “Slay and there is no harm.” He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was not asked. About something that was brought forward and not delayed except that he said: Do it and there is no problem.”"
"3995","Ali bin Hajar told me, he said: Ismail informed me, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ka`b ibn Ajra, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to me at the time of Hudaybiyyah, and I was making a fire under a pot and lice were scattered on my forehead or My eyebrows. He said: Are your worries bothering you? I said: Yes. He said: Shave your head and keep yourself clean, or fast for three days or feed. “Six poor people.” He said, “I don’t know what happened to them.”"
"3996","Amr ibn Ali reported, saying: Azhar ibn Saad told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ujra, He said: “This verse was revealed about me, so I came to him, and he said: Come closer, so I approached, and he said: Are your worries bothering you? I said: Yes, so he ordered me to fast.” Or charity or rituals.” Ibn Awf said: Mujahid explained it to me, so I asked Ayoub, and he said: Fasting for three days, and giving charity for six days. Poor people, and rituals as long as possible"
"3997","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Mu’tamar told us, saying: I heard Saif, a man from the people of Mecca, speaking on the authority of a mujahid, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman. Ibn Abi Laila, that Ka’b told him, saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, stood over me in Al-Hudaybiyyah while my head was covered with lice, and he said: Do your worries bother you? I said: Yes, O Messenger of God. He said: So shave your head. This verse was revealed: Whoever of you is sick or has a disease? If he hurts his head, then a ransom of fasting, charity, or rituals. He said: And the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded me and said: Fast for three days. Or give in charity a sweat of six or a sheep as much as possible. He said: And God revealed this about it. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3998","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna and Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Muhammad told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Isbahani, on the authority of Abd Allah ibn Maqil said: “I sat from this mosque to Ka’b ibn Ujrah, and I asked him about this verse: a ransom for fasting.” He said Ka'b: I descended on my head, and I had an injury on my head, so I was carried to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, while lice were scattered on my face. He said: I was not. I see that your effort is reaching what I see. You find a sheep? I said: No, so this verse was revealed: So it is a ransom of fasting, charity, or rituals. Fasting is for three days, and alms is given to six poor people, for each poor person half a saa’ of food.” In the hadith of Ibn Bashar, and the rituals are a sheep. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"3999","Qutaybah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, shaved and a group of His companions, and some of them fell short, and Ibn Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: May God have mercy on those who shave, once or twice, then He said: And those who fall short."
"4000","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abd al-Razzaq reported, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, “that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He shaved his head during his Hajj."
"4001","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id reported, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who said: “He has mercy May God have mercy on those who cut their hair. They said: O Messenger of God, and those who fall short? He said: May God have mercy on those who cut their hair. He said, meaning in the fourth verse: And those who fall short. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4002","Al-Hussein bin Harith told Abu Ammar, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, he said: “When he threw The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered his sacrifice, then gave the barber his right side, and he shaved it. He gave it to Abu Talha, then gave him his right side. He shaved it off and said: Divide it among the people."
"4003","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman, who said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Husayn, on the authority of his grandmother, who was Husayn’s mother, who said: I heard the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “O God, forgive those who shave,” they said: And those who fall short. He said: “O God, forgive those who shave,” they said: And the negligent ones. He said: And the negligent ones. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4004","Muhammad ibn Aban al-Balkhi reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Hujayr, on the authority of Tawus, he said: Ibn Abbas said: Muawiyah said to me: Did you know that I cut the head of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, with a hair clip? I said: No. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4005","Ya’qub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Ja’far bin Muhammad told us, he said: My father told me, he said: “We came to Jabir bin Abdullah, so he told us that the group of guidance that Ali brought from Yemen, and that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, brought at his door, so the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave sixty-three things and gave Ali, so he slaughtered whatever he had not found, and joined him in his sacrifice. Then he ordered from each camel a few So it was put in a pot, and they ate of its flesh and drank of its broth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4006","Shuaib bin Yusuf reported, on the authority of Yahya ibn Sa’id, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, who said: Ata’ told us, and Ya’qub bin Ibrahim reported, saying: He told us Hushaym, who said: Abd al-Malik told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “We used to have fun with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we would slaughter a cow on the “Seven in which we share.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4007","Abu Dawud reported, saying: Affan told us, saying: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace And he slaughtered the camel at the age of seven and the cow at the age of seven.”"
"4008","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “We sacrificed with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Al-Hudaybiyyah.” A camel for seven, and a cow for seven.”"
"4009","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Al-Fadl bin Musa told us, he said: Al-Hussein bin Waqid told us, on the authority of Alba bin Ahmar, on the authority of Ikrimah On the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he attended the sacrifice, so we slaughtered ten camels.”"
"4010","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan reported, saying: Waki’ told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abaya bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of his grandfather Rafi’ bin Khadij, He said: “We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in Dhul-Hulayfah, from Tihama, and we struck sheep and camels, and the people ran away, meaning before... The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and ordered it to be done, and it was rewarded. Then he equalized ten of the sheep with carrots, then he A camel was beaten, and there were only a few horses among the people. A man shot an arrow and caught it. The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: These animals have backs. Like the animals of the wild beast, so whatever is upon you, do thus to them.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4011","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Saeed, who was Ibn Masruq, on the authority of Abaya bin Rifa’ah, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, who said: We were with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and the people quickly came forward and hurried away some of the spoils, so they cooked while the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, At the end of the people, he passed by the pots and ordered them to be filled, then he divided among them and equaled a camel with ten sheep. One of the people’s camels ran out, but there was no They had horses with them, and a man shot him with an arrow and caught him. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, these animals have creatures like animals.” If the beast does this, then do this to it.”"
"4012","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Othman bin Omar told us, saying: Yunus reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He, peace and blessings be upon him, sacrificed a cow on behalf of his wives during the Farewell Pilgrimage. Uthman said: I found it in this book of mine in two places: a place about Umrah. On the authority of Aisha, and on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4013","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, saying: Yunus informed me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Amra bint Abd al-Rahman. On the authority of Aisha, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sacrificed one cow on behalf of the family of Muhammad during the Farewell Pilgrimage.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4014","Amr bin Uthman told me, he said: Al-Walid told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: “He slaughtered The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on the authority of one of his wives who performed Umrah with him during the Farewell Pilgrimage, gave a cow among them.”"
"4015","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Ubayd Allah told us, saying: Israel told us, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered a cow for us on the day of our Hajj.”"
"4016","Muhammad bin Rafi’ reported, saying: Abdul Razzaq told us, saying: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “What was slaughtered On the authority of the family of Muhammad during the Farewell Pilgrimage, except for a cow.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4017","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Ibn Abi Zaida, who said: Yahya bin Saeed reported, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “A day has come upon us. Slaughtering beef, so I said: What is this? It was said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered on behalf of his wives. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4018","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik ibn Anas told me, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed said: Amra bint Abdul Rahman told me that she heard Aisha say: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave orders for five nights before him, may God bless him and grant him peace. And the one who did not have a sacrificial animal was greeted when he circumambulated the Kaaba and ran between Safa and Marwah to make it permissible. Aisha said: And the Day of Sacrifice has entered upon us. With beef, I said: What is this? They said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered the meat on behalf of his wives. Yahya said: So I mentioned this hadith. To Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, and he said: She brought you the hadith according to its authenticity. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4019","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Jafar bin Muhammad, he said: My father told us, he said: Jabir told us, he said: The Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “All of Mina is slaughtered.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4020","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, on the authority of Hushaym, he said: Yunus bin Ubaid reported, saying: Ibn Jubayr told me, he said: “I was with Ibn Umar at Mina, and he passed by A man slaughtered his camel while it was blessed, and he said: Send it standing, tied, according to the Sunnah of Abu Al-Qasim, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"4021","Ahmad bin Sulaiman reported, saying: Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, saying: Israel reported, about a partition, he said: Najiya bin Jundub told me. Al-Aslami said, “He came to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, when the sacrificial animal was blocked, and said: O Messenger of God, send him with me and I will slaughter him.” He said: How? He said: He took him through valleys beyond which he could pass. He said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pushed him and took him off until we slaughtered him in the Sacred Mosque. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4022","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, on the authority of Ibn Ulayya, who said: Abu al-Tayyah told us, on the authority of Musa bin Salamah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, May God bless him and grant him peace. He sent eighteen camels with a man and ordered him to go. Then he returned to him and said: What do you think if any of them creeps upon us? He said: Slaughter it, then dye its soles with its blood, then put it on its surface, and neither you nor any of your companions may eat from it. \""
"4023","Harun bin Ishaq reported, saying: Abdah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Najiya Al-Khuza’i, he said: “I said: O Messenger of God, how? What should I do with what is damaged from the body? He said: Slaughter it, then dip its soles in its blood, then leave it among the people so that they may eat it."
"4024","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Ataa told us, he said: I heard Jabir, he said: “We used not to eat meat.” There were only three of us, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave us permission, so we ate and took our supplies.” I said: Jabir said: Until we returned to Medina. He said: No"
"4025","Ali bin Hajar reported, saying: Ismail told us, saying: Ja`far bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered one hundred camels, of which the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered sixty-three camels, and Ali slaughtered what was left, then he ordered The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, to take a small portion from each camel and put it in a pot, and they ate from its meat and sipped from its broth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4026","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, on the authority of Shuaib, he said: Al-Layth reported, on the authority of Ibn al-Haad, on the authority of Ja’far bin Muhammad, on the authority of His father, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, said: “Ali came from Yemen with a gift for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and it was the gift that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and Ali brought from Yemen one hundred camels, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered sixty-three of them. And Ali slaughtered thirty-seven, and joined Ali in his body, then a small amount was taken from each body and put in a pot and cooked, and the Messenger of God ate it. May God’s prayers and peace be upon him and Ali from its meat and drink from its broth.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4027","Imran bin Yazid told us, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told me, he said: Ata told me, that he heard Jabir, saying: “We were not “We eat from the flesh of the body, except for three.” The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, granted us permission and said: “Eat and provide for yourself.” So we ate and provided for ourselves."
"4028","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Saif bin Sulaiman told us, he said: I heard Mujahid, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin told me. Abu Laila said: I heard Ali saying: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to take care of his body and to give its meat in charity.” So I gave in charity, and he ordered me to give in charity their skins, so I gave in charity, and he ordered me to give in charity their skins, so I gave in charity.”"
"4029","Imran bin Yazid told me, he said: Shuaib bin Ishaq told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told me, he said: Hassan bin Muslim told me, that Mujahid told him: that Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila told him, that Ali bin Abi Talib told him, “that the Messenger of God, may God bless him He commanded him to take care of his body and ordered him to distribute his entire body, its meat, skins, and skins, among the poor, and not to give to the poor. “I cut off some of it.” I said to Al-Hasan: “Who should this be divided into?” He said: No"
"4030","Imran bin Yazid told me, he said: Shuaib told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told me, he said: Abdul Karim bin Malik told me, that Mujahid He told him: That Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila told him that Ali bin Abi Talib told him that “the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded him.” That he should take charge of his body, and that he should divide the entire body, its meat, skins, and skins, and not give any of it to the one who slaughtered it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4031","Amr bin Ali reported, saying: Yahya told us, saying: Ibn Jurayj told us, saying: Al-Hasan bin Muslim and Abd al-Karim al-Jazari told me, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to take care of his body and to give alms.” With their meat and skins, and that I do not give anything from their butchering.”"
"4032","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to attend to its body and ordered me to divide its skins and its glory, and he ordered me not to I gave the butcher some of it.”"
"4033","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to take care of his body and ordered me to divide its skins and its glory.”"
"4034","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told me, he said: Muadh bin Hisham told me, he said: My father told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, On the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to divide the body, then he said: I swear So I said: Yes. He said: Divide her camels and her skins."
"4035","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, on the authority of Abdul Wahhab, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abdul Karim, and Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdul Al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent with him his gift and ordered him to give its meat and skins as alms.” \"And I deferred it\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4036","Muhammad bin Adam told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahim, meaning Ibn Sulaiman, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to look for the body. He ordered me to do so, and I divided its skins and skins, then He ordered me to divide its meat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4037","Muhammad ibn Adam told me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahim, on the authority of Sufyan al-Thawri, on the authority of Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, sent me to take care of the body and ordered me not to give anything of it to her.” \"Her butchery\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4038","Ishaq bin Mansour reported, he said: Abdul Rahman reported, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded him to take care of the body, and he commanded him not to give any of it to the slaughterer because he slaughtered her.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4039","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Muadh bin Muadh told us, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abd al-Karim al-Jazari told us, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded me to take care of his body and to give its meat in charity.” And their skins and their hides, and that I should not be given the reward of a butcher of them, and he said: We will give him from us.” He said: Sufyan Al-Thawri told me, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Abi Laila, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he did not say: “We will give it from ourselves.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4040","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “We used to provide ourselves with sacrificial meat during the reign of The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, to Medina.”"
"4041","Muhammad bin Abdul-Ala reported, saying: Khaled told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said regarding sacrificial meat: “ We were going to Medina with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4042","Amr bin Ali reported, on the authority of Ibn Mahdi, who said: Muawiyah bin Saleh told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zahiriyah, on the authority of Jubayr bin Nufayr, on the authority of Thawban, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, slaughtered his sacrifice, then he said: O Thuban, prepare the meat of this sheep, so I fed him.” From there until we came to Medina.”"
"4043","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I did good to the Messenger of God.” May God’s blessings and peace be upon him in my hand before it overflows.”"
"4044","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, he said: Yazid told us, he said: Yahya reported, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard Aisha, She says: “I perfumed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in his sanctuary, and I perfumed him in Mina before it flooded.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4045","Al-Mughirah bin Abdul-Rahman told me, he said: Isa told us, he is Ibn Yunus, he said: Al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Al-Qasim, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I congratulated the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for his ihram when he entered ihram and for his permissibility when he entered ihram before it overflowed.” \"Home\""
"4046","Ayyub ibn Muhammad al-Wazzan reported, saying: Omar ibn Ayyub told us, saying: Aflah ibn Humayd reported, on the authority of Abu Bakr, that Suleiman ibn Abd The king, in the year of Hajj, gathered people of knowledge, including Omar bin Abdul Aziz, Kharijah bin Zayd bin Thabit, and Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, And Salem, and Abdullah ibn Abdullah, and Ibn Shihab, and Abu Bakr, so he asked them about perfume before eating, and they all told him about perfume. Al-Qasim said: Aisha told me, “She perfumed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for his sanctity when he entered ihram and for his permissibility before he circumambulated.” In the House,” and none of them disagreed over him except Abdullah, who said: Abdullah was a serious and diligent man who would stone the Jamarat and then He slaughters, then shave, then mounts and runs before he comes to his house. Salem said: He is right. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4047","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Ibn Ulayya reported, on the authority of Ayoub, saying: I heard Al-Qasim bin Muhammad saying: Aisha said: “I was good to the Messenger of God.” May God bless him and grant him peace.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4048","Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Da’eef reported, saying: Abdul-Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “ “I was kind to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for his permissibility and his prohibition.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4049","Abdullah bin Muhammad reported, saying: Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I used to perfume The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, declared it sacred before it became ihram and permitted it before it overflowed.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4050","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, he said: I heard Al-Qasim, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “I did good to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” And peace be upon him for his wife when he entered ihram and for his wife when he entered ihram at Mina before he circumambulated the Kaaba.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4051","Harun bin Musa reported, saying: Abu Damra told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, She said: “I perfumed the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for his ihram before he entered ihram and for his permissibility before he poured water.”"
"4052","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abd al-Razzaq reported, he said: Muammar told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: When he shot and shaved Everything is permissible for him except women and perfume. Salem said: Aisha used to say: “He has everything except women. I was good to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"4053","Ibrahim bin Harun Al-Balkhi told me, he said: Hatim bin Ismail told us, he said: Ja’far bin Muhammad bin Ali bin Hussein told us, on the authority of His father, he said: We entered upon Jabir bin Abdullah, and I said, “Tell me about the proof of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace.” He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, elaborated.” May God bless him and grant him peace, he went home and prayed the noon prayer in Mecca, so he came to the Banu Abdul Muttalib to water Zamzam, and he said: Remove the Banu Abdul Muttalib. If the people had not prevailed upon you to give you something to drink, I would have gone with you. So they handed him a bucket and he drank from it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4054","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abdul Razzaq reported, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace He performed the salaam for a portion of the Day of Sacrifice, then returned and performed the noon prayer at Mina.”"
"4055","Muhammad bin Al-Muthanna reported, saying: Abdul Rahman told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Aisha, and Ibn Abbas, “that the Prophet prayed May God bless him and grant him peace, he delayed the circumambulation on the Day of Sacrifice until nightfall.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4056","Yunus ibn Abd al-Ala and al-Harith ibn Miskin reported on the authority of Ibn Wahb, who said: Ibn Juraij told us, on the authority of Ata bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, did not have sand during the seven days in which he had intercourse.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4057","Hilal bin Al-Ala reported, saying: Hajjaj told us, saying: Hammad told us, on the authority of Qays bin Saad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Jabir, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came May God bless him and grant him peace for four days during the month of Dhul-Hijjah. When he circumambulated the House, Safa, and Marwah, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Make it an Umrah, and when it was the Day of Tarwiyah they declared the Hajj Akbar, but when it was the Day of Sacrifice they came and circumambulated the Kaaba, but they did not circumambulate between Safa and Marwah.”"
"4058","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Malik told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “The companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Those who were with him did not circumambulate during Hajj until they stoned the Jamarat.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4059","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “The companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace “Those who performed Ihram for Umrah circumambulated the House, Safa, and Marwah, then they circumambulated after they returned from Mina for their Hajj.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4060","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told me, he said: I am Ashhab, that Malik told them: that Ibn Shihab and Hisham bin Urwa They told him, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “We went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in the year of the Farewell Pilgrimage, so we came to Mecca. So those who had qualified for Umrah circumambulated the House, Safa, and Marwah, then they came out of ihram, then they performed another circumambulation after they returned from Mina for their Hajj. As for those who combined Hajj and Umrah, they only performed one circumambulation.” Abu Abd al-Rahman said: No one said anything, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, other than Ashhab, and God knows best. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4061","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Ibn Abi Zaida, he said: Malik bin Anas reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, “that the companions of The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not circumambulate the Kaaba and between Safa and Marwah until they returned from Mina.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4062","Imran ibn Yazid informed me, he said: Shuaib informed me, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: Abu al-Zubayr informed me, that he heard Jabir ibn Abdullah He says: “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and his companions did not circumambulate between Safa and Marwah except once, the first circumambulation.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4063","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Issa bin Yunus reported, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permitted May God grant him peace and grant that Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib spend the night in Mecca during the days of Mina in order to provide him with water."
"4064","Ishaq bin Mansour reported, he said: Abdul Rahman reported, on the authority of Malik, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Al-Baddah bin Asim bin Adiy, on the authority of his father, “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, gave permission for camel herders in the house near Mina to throw stones on the Day of Sacrifice. Then they will shoot tomorrow and two days after tomorrow, then they will shoot on the Day of Departure.”"
"4065","Muhammad ibn Salamah reported, saying: Ibn Wahb told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, he said: Ubayd Allah ibn Abdullah ibn Umar informed me, on the authority of His father, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed two rak’ahs in Mina, and Abu Bakr prayed two rak’ahs there.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4066","Muhammad bin Bashar reported, saying: Sahl bin Yusuf and Hammad bin Masada told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Bukayr bin Ata, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Yamar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “He was asked about Hajj, and he said: Hajj is Arafat, three days. two days, there is no sin on him, and whoever delays it, there is no sin on him.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4067","Al-Hussein bin Harith told Abu Ammar, he said: Saeed bin Salem told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ali, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Uqba bin Amir, that the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, he said: “The Day of Arafat and the Day of Sacrifice, and the days of Tashreeq for us, the people of Islam, are days of eating and drinking.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4068","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, on the authority of Hushaym, and Ibn Ulayyah, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Malih, on the authority of Nubaysha al-Hudhali, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “The days of Tashreeq are days of eating, drinking, and remembrance of God.”"
"4069","Abu Dawud reported, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Yazid ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Ata’, speaking on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “I was among those who wasted the weight of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, in two days,” and Ata’ said: And I will do it."
"4070","Muhammad ibn Mansour reported, saying: Sufyan told us, saying: Sulayman al-Ahwal and al-Harith ibn Miskin told us, a reading from him while I was hearing, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Suleiman Al-Ahwal, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “No one should leave until he has His last pledge was circumambulation of the Kaaba, and the word is for Muhammad. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4071","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Ali bin Ata, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Abdul Rahman, he said: Al-Harith bin Abdullah: “I came to Omar ibn al-Khattab and asked him about a woman who circumambulates the Kaaba and then menstruates? He said: That will be her last period in the Kaaba. He said: Al-Harith: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, gave me a fatwa. Omar said: I am like that. You asked me about what you asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. peace be upon him, while I disagree with him.”"
"4072","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Sufyan reported, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “Safiyya had her menstruation, so I mentioned that.” to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Did she imprison us? I said: No, she had had her bleeding and then had her period. He said: Then no?"
"4073","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Salamah, and Urwa, that Aisha said: “Safiya had her menstruation.” Bint Huyayy after she had menstruation. Aisha said: So I mentioned her menstruation to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: Did she imprison us? So I said: Oh Messenger of God, she had had an intercourse and had circumambulated the Kaaba, then she had her period after the intercourse. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Let her go away."
"4074","Abd al-Malik ibn Shuaib ibn al-Layth ibn Saad reported, saying: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: Ja`far ibn Rabi’ah told me, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Hurmuz, on the authority of Abu Salamah, that Aisha said: “We performed Hajj with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we performed Hajj on the Day of Sacrifice.” Safiyya menstruated, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted from her what a man wants from his family, so she said: O Messenger of God, she is menstruating. He said: Did she imprison us? They said: O Messenger of God, she made her sacrifice on the Day of Sacrifice. He said: Come out."
"4075","Suleiman bin Ubayd Allah bin Amr Al-Ghaylani Al-Basri reported, saying: Umayyah told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: Ibrahim told us, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, “Safiya had her period after circumambulating the Kaaba on the Day of Sacrifice, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered her to \"repel\""
"4076","Mahmoud bin Ghaylan reported, saying: Yahya bin Adam told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha. The wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Safiya had her menstrual period before leaving, so she asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: I had performed a tawaf. On the Day of Sacrifice? She said: Yes, so he ordered her to leave. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4077","Muhammad bin Qudamah told me, on the authority of Jarir, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha. Safiya said: “He did not show me Unless I will detain you. He said: My neck or my throat, or have I not circumambulated on the Day of Sacrifice? She said: Yes. He said: No problem, go away? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4078","Muhammad ibn al-Muthanna and Muhammad ibn Bashar reported on the authority of Muhammad, who said: Shu`bah told us, on the authority of al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha said: “When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wanted to leave, he saw Safiya at the door of her hiding place, depressed or sad, and then she menstruated. Then the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Aqra or shaved, you have detained us. Did you disperse on the Day of Sacrifice?” She said: “Yes.” He said: “Then go away.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4079","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, who said: “I mentioned to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said that Safiyya bint Huyayy menstruated during the days of Mina, and he said: Did she imprison us? They said: She had menstruated, so he said: Did she imprison us? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Then no.”"
"4080","Muhammad ibn Salamah and al-Harith ibn Miskin narrated a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn al-Qasim, who said: Malik narrated to me, on the authority of Abdullah Bin Abi Bakr bin Muhammad bin Amr bin Hazm, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Amra, on the authority of Aisha, that she said to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “O Messenger of God, Safiyya bint Huyayy has menstruated, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Perhaps she will detain us. Didn’t Did she circumambulate the Kaaba with you? They said: Yes. He said: So go out. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4081","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Ismail told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin al-Qasim, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, “that Safiyya had her menstruation after she had had her menstruation, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: She has detained us, so Aisha said: She has had her menstruation. He said: \"Then no\""
"4082","Ishaq bin Ibrahim told us, he said: Issa bin Yunus told us, he said: Ubayd Allah told us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: “Whoever performs Hajj, let another His stay at home, except for menstruating women, whom the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permitted.”"
"4083","Amr bin Ali reported, saying: Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, saying: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Maysara, he said: I heard Tawus talking, on the authority of Ibn Omar, that he used to say, close to the time of sixty: “Do not leave until her last visit to the Kaaba is.” Then Ibn Omar said afterward: “She should leave, for it was permitted.” \"for women\" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4084","Abdul-Malik bin Shuaib bin Al-Layth bin Saad reported, saying: My father told me, on the authority of my grandfather, he said: Aqeel told us, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Tawus. Al-Yamani, that he narrated to him, that he heard Abdullah bin Omar, “and he was being asked about imprisoning women, for circumambulating the Kaaba if they had menstruated before The group, and the Day of Sacrifice was over, and he said: Aisha used to mention on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he granted permission to women, and that A year before the death of Abdullah bin Omar"
"4085","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Yazid, Al-Harith bin Miskin, reported a reading to him while I was listening, and the wording is Muhammad’s, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, said: “The people were commanded that their last period of time should be with the House, except that it was permitted for the menstruating woman.” \" (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4086","Ja`far bin Musafir reported, he said: Yahya bin Hassan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Ibn Tawus told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, He said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permitted a menstruating woman to go away when she has had an intercourse.” Tawus said: And I heard Ibn Umar say: “ If the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, repel them, he granted them permission.”"
"4087","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Muslim told me, on the authority of Tawus, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas, and Zaid bin Thabit said to him: Are you the one who gives the fatwa to a menstruating woman to leave before her last visit to the House? Ibn Abbas said to him: Ask so-and-so Ansari woman, did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, order her to leave? So he asked her, then he came back laughing and said: The story is as you told me."
"4088","Mahmoud bin Khalid told me, he said: Omar, who is Ibn Abdul-Wahid, told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Al-Zuhri told me, on the authority of Abu Salamah On the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said when he wanted to leave Mina: “We will camp tomorrow, God willing, in fear of the children of Kinanah, meaning Al-Muhasab, “and that is because the Quraysh and the Banu Kinanah took an oath among the Banu Hashim and the Banu Abdul Muttalib not to marry them and not to have There was something between them and them until they submitted to them the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"4089","Musa bin Abdul Rahman reported, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Zaida, he said: Malik bin Mughal told us, on the authority of Awn bin Abi Juhayfah, on the authority of His father, he said: “I was sent to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was in Al-Abtah in Qobba. When he was in Al-Hijra, Bilal came out and called for prayer, then Bilal entered and took out the goat, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came out, as if I were looking at the whiteness of his legs. He set the goat down and established the prayer. He led us in two rak'ahs of noon prayer and two rak'ahs of afternoon prayer, and a woman and a donkey passed in front of him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4090","Sulaiman bin Dawud and Al-Harith bin Miskin narrated a reading from him while I was listening, on the authority of Ibn Wahb. He said: Amr bin Al-Harith narrated to me. That Qatada narrated to him, that Anas bin Malik narrated to him, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, prayed the noon, afternoon, sunset, and evening prayers and slept.” He lay down, then he rode to the House and walked around it.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4091","Al-Abbas bin Muhammad reported, he said: Al-Ahwas bin Jawab told us, he said: Ammar told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered from Batha on the night of the departure.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4092","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told us, and Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abdul Razzaq told us, he said: Muammar told, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, that Ibn Omar used to visit Al-Abtah. Al-Zuhri said: Urwa told me, on the authority of Aisha, “She was not She preferred that, and said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, only revealed it because this was the one that allowed it to come out,” and the wording is for Muhammad. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4093","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Issa bin Yunus reported, saying: Hisham bin Urwa told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: “Al-Muhasab is not “Indeed, it is a revelation sent down by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, so that it may allow its emergence.”"
"4094","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Abdullah bin Dawud told us, he said: Al-Hasan bin Saleh told us, he said: I asked Amr bin Dinar about Al-Muhassab. Al-Abtah, and he said: Ibn Abbas said: “It was only a residence sent down by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"4095","Ali bin Hajar reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: “Al-Muhassab is not a thing, but he is A place sent down by the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.”"
"4096","Ziyad bin Ayyub told me, he said: Ismail bin Aliya told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Ishaq told us, he said: I asked Anas bin Malik about He shortened the prayer and said: “We traveled with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, from Medina to Mecca, and he prayed two rak’ahs for us until we returned.” So I asked him: Did he stay in Mecca? He said: Yes, he stayed in Mecca for ten days."
"4097","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, he said: I asked Urwa bin Al-Zubayr, “How long did the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, stay in prayer?” In Mecca? He said: Ten. I said: Ibn Abbas claims that he stayed for a few ten days. He said: Ibn Abbas lied. He said: So he hated him. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4098","Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak reported, saying: Yahya told us, on the authority of Abdul-Rahman bin Humaid bin Abdul-Rahman, he said: I heard Omar bin Abdul Aziz asks Al-Sa'ib bin Yazid: What did you hear about the people living in Mecca? He said: Al-Alaa bin Al-Hadrami told us that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The immigrant has three after the chest.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4099","Ubayd Allah bin Saad bin Ibrahim bin Saad told us, he said: My uncle told us, he said: My father told us, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Hamid, that he heard Omar bin Abdul Aziz, asking Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid, and Al-Sa’ib said: I heard Al-Ala’ bin Al-Hadrami, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, says: “The immigrant stays for three nights in Mecca after al-Sadr.”"
"4100","Muhammad bin Rafi’ told us, he said: Abd al-Razzaq told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Ismail bin Muhammad bin Saad informed me, that Humaid bin Abdul Rahman bin Awf told him that Al-Sa’ib bin Yazid told him that he heard Al-Ala bin Al-Hadrami say: The Messenger of God said God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “The immigrant stays in Mecca after performing his rituals for three days.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4101","Amr ibn Zurarah reported, he said: Ismail reported, he said: Ayoub reported, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Bakra, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace He addressed his argument and said: “Indeed, time has turned around as it was on the day God created the heavens and the earth. The year has twelve months of it.” “Four sacred places, three in succession: Dhul-Qa’dah, Dhul-Hijjah, Muharram, and Rajab, which is between Jumada and Sha’ban.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4102","Al-Hasan bin Mudrak reported, saying: Yahya bin Hammad told us, saying: Abu Awanah told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abdullah Al-Awdi, he said: Tell me Humaid bin Abdul Rahman Al-Himyari said: Ahban Ibn Abu Dharr’s wife told me, he said: I asked Abu Dharr, I said: Which of the necks is purer? ? Which night is best? Which months are best? Abu Dharr said: I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, as you asked me, and I will tell you as he told me. I said: O Messenger of God, which necks? Is it smarter? Which night is best? Which months are best? He said to me: “The purest of slaves is the most expensive, the best of the night is its hollow, and the best of months is the month of God, which you call Muharram.”"
"4103","Muhammad ibn Qudamah told me, he said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: I and Urwa ibn al-Zubayr entered the mosque, Then Abdullah bin Omar, sitting in Aisha’s room, said: How many times did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform the Umrah? She said: Four. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4104","Abu Dawud reported, saying: Al-Hasan told us, he is Ibn Muhammad bin Ayan, he said: Zuhair told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Mujahid, “that Ibn Umar was asked: How many times did the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, perform the Umrah? He said: Twice. Aisha said: Ibn Umar knew that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Umrah. May God bless him and grant him peace. He has performed three Umrahs, in addition to the Umrah which he associated with the Farewell Pilgrimage.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4105","Ibrahim bin Yaqoub told me, he said: Yahya bin Ya’la told us, he said: My father told us, he said: Ghaylan bin Jami’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, said: Ibn Abi Awfa said: “I performed Umrah with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he took possession of the stone and circumambulated for a week, and circumambulated between Safa and Marwah, so we used to cover the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for fear that some of the people of Mecca would shoot him.”"
"4106","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, he said: Ismail told us, he said: Ibn Abi Awfa told us, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed the Umrah May God bless him and grant him peace. He circumambulated the Kaaba, then he went out between Safa and Marwah, circling around, and We made us protect him from the people of Mecca lest any of them throw him. Or something befalls him.”"
"4107","Ishaq bin Ibrahim reported, he said: Jarir reported, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Urwa bin al-Zubayr and I entered, and Urwa said To Aisha: Ibn Omar says: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed Umrah in Rajab.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4108","Imran ibn Yazid informed me, he said: Shuaib informed me, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, he said: I heard Ata’, saying: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me, he said: “ I and Ibn Umar were leaning in Aisha’s room. We could hear her voice as she was cleaning herself with the siwak, so I said to him: O Abu Abd al-Rahman. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed Umrah in Rajab. He said: Yes. I said to Aisha: O mother, do you not hear what Abu Abdul Rahman says? She said: What does he say? I said: He says: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed Umrah in Rajab. She said: May God forgive Abu Abdul Rahman for what he performed Umrah in Rajab. Rajab, and he did not perform the Umrah except that he stayed with him, and Ibn Umar was listening, so he did not say “no” or “yes,” he remained silent.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4109","Humayd bin Masada reported, saying: Sufyan bin Habib told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, he said: I heard Ibn Abbas, saying: A prophet said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said to a woman from the Ansar: “What prevented you from performing Hajj with us?” She said: O Messenger of God, we had two water-drinkers, so Abu So-and-so went to her husband, and her son went to a watering can, so they rode on it and left for us a watering hole to sprinkle on. Then the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Then “It is Ramadan, so perform Umrah, for Umrah is equivalent to Hajj.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4110","Qutayba bin Saeed reported, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ibn al-Munkadir, he said: I heard Yusuf bin Abdullah bin Salam, he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said He, peace and blessings be upon him, said to a man from the Ansar and his wife: “Perform Umrah during Ramadan, for Umrah therein is for you as a Hajj.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4111","Ubayd Allah bin Saeed reported, saying: Yahya bin Adam told us, saying: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Bayan, and another mentioned, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Wahb bin Khanbash Al-Ta’i, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Umrah in Ramadan is equivalent to Hajj.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4112","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, Hisham bin Abi Abdullah told us, he said: Yahya bin Abi Kathir told me, on the authority of Abu Salamah Bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Maqil bin Umm Maqil, who said: “My mother wanted to perform Hajj and her camel was weak, so she asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “Perform Umrah during Ramadan, for Umrah during it is equivalent to Hajj.”"
"4113","Muhammad ibn Rafi’ reported, saying: Abd al-Razzaq told us, saying: Mu’mar reported, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, on the authority of a woman from Banu Asad, called Umm Maqil, said: “I wanted to perform Hajj because of the surplus of my camel, so I asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He greeted him and said: “Perform Umrah in the month of Ramadan, for Umrah in the month of Ramadan is equivalent to Hajj.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4114","Muhammad bin Yahya bin Muhammad bin Kathir al-Harrani reported, saying: Omar bin Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of his father, he said: Al-A’mash told us, he said: Amara and Jami’ bin Shaddad told me, on the authority of Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al Harith bin Hisham, on the authority of Abu Maqil, “He came To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: Umm Maqil made a proof against her with you, but that was not possible for her, so what will be sufficient for her? He said: Umrah in Ramadan. He said: I have a camel that I kept prisoner for the sake of God, so I should give it to her so she can ride it. He said: Yes? (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4115","Ishaq bin Ibrahim narrated, he said: Abd al-Razzaq narrated, he said: Muammar narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of his father, he said: “Umrah in The months of Hajj are complete. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, followed them and God revealed them in His Book."
"4116","Ubayd Allah ibn Sa`id reported, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Amr, he said: Amr ibn Aws informed me, he said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi informed me Bakr, he said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to accompany Aisha and give her a lifetime of comfort.”"
"4117","Hanad bin Al-Sari reported, on the authority of Ibn Abi Zaida, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, that Aisha, She said to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace: “I find within myself that during my lifetime I have not performed tawaaf.” He said: “Then go with it, O Abdul Rahman.” So fill it with bliss.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4118","Muhammad ibn Abd al-Ala informed us, saying: Al-Mu`tamir told us, saying: I heard Ayman, meaning Ibn Nabul, speaking on the authority of al-Qasim ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: “O Messenger of God, your women go out for Umrah and Hajj, and I go out for Hajj.” He said to her brother Abd al-Rahman: “Make it full of bliss.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4119","And while Ahmad bin Mani’ read to us, he said: Ismail told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad and Ibn Aoun, On the authority of Al-Qasim, Al-Hasan bin Muhammad Al-Zaafrani reported, he said: Hussein bin Hassan told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Al-Qasim, on the authority of Umm believers, because she said: “O Messenger of God, will people perform two rituals and I will perform one ritual.” He said: Wait, and when you are pure So go out to Al-Tan’im and be my family there, then bring us such-and-such mountain.” And the pronunciation is good. Ahmad said in his hadith: On the authority of Ismail: He said Ibn Aoun: I do not memorize this hadith from that hadith. (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4120","Al-Harith bin Miskin, I read about it while I was listening, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, on the authority of Muzahim, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Abdullah bin Khalid, on the authority of Muhrish al-Kaabi, said: “I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, come out of al-Jirana at night, and I looked at Its back was as if it were a silver alloy, so it was melted and became silver with it.”"
"4121","Qutaibah bin Saeed reported, saying: Saeed bin Muzahim bin Abi Muzahim told us, saying: Abi Muzahim bin Abi Muzahim told me, on the authority of Abdul Aziz Ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Muhrish al-Kaabi, said: “The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered al-Ji’ranah, and the people of al-Ji’ranah knew of his entrance, so they gathered together.” And they increased, and it was as if I was looking at the whiteness of his armpit and side, as if the whiteness of it were silver bars. He raised his hands, then said: O people. To you on my behalf, so they moved away from him until he came to the mosque, and he bowed as long as God wished, then entered into ihram, then he mounted his mount and faced the belly of He traveled on until he met the road to Mecca, and he spent the morning in Mecca like a woman.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4122","Amr bin Ali told us, he said: Yahya told us, he said: Ibn Jurayj told us, he said: Muzahim bin Abi Muzahim told me, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Abdul God, on the authority of Muhrish al-Kaabi, “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, left al-Jirana performing Umrah at night, entered Mecca at night, and performed his Umrah.” Then he came out from the depths of his night, and became in a ji'ranah like a turban, and when the sun had set the next day, he came out from the belly of a si'raf until he came along the road. The road to Medina was surrounded by Saraf, and for this reason its umrah was hidden from many people.”"
"4123","Issa bin Hammad reported, he said: Al-Layth reported, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Rabah, on the authority of Ibn Munya, on the authority of his father, “that a man came To the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He had entered ihram for Umrah and was wearing a Jibbah, and he was in his robes. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered him to He took it off completely, bathed two or three times, and said: “Whatever you did in your Hajj, do it in your Umrah.”"
"4124","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, saying: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ali bin Umayyah, he said: “A Bedouin came to the Prophet and prayed. May God bless him and grant him peace, and he was wearing a robe with a saffron overlay, and he said: O Messenger of God, as you can see I have entered ihram while the people are mocking me. So he looked away from him for a while, then called him and said: Take off this robe, wash off this saffron, and do as you do in your Umrah. “What you do during your Hajj,” and Ya’qub told us, saying: Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ya’la ibn Umayyah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace, like that (Peace Be Upon Him)"
"4125","Yaqoub bin Ibrahim reported, on the authority of Ibn Ulayya, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: “When Ibn Umar entered the closest part of the Haram, he remained silent. He recites the talbiyah, then spends the night in Dhu Tuwa, then performs the morning prayer there and washes himself, and it is said that the Prophet of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do that.” (Peace Be Upon Him)"
